<article class="env-lemma" id="0AUC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AUC">Lemma <span data-tag="0AUC">48.20.7</span>.</a> Let $(S, \omega _ S^\bullet )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/0AU4" data-tag="0AU4">48.20.1</a>. Let $j : X \to Y$ be an open immersion of schemes of finite type over $S$. Let $\omega _ X^\bullet $ and $\omega _ Y^\bullet $ be dualizing complexes normalized relative to $\omega _ S^\bullet $. Then there is a canonical isomorphism $\omega _ X^\bullet = \omega _ Y^\bullet |_ X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the construction of normalized dualizing complexes given just above Definition <a href="/tag/0AUA" data-tag="0AUA">48.20.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>